<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46737" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭper-illĭno</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-inl-</span></b> ), no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
			lĭtum (collat. form superillinītum,
					<i><span class="en">App. Herb. 74</span></i>),
			3, v. a.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To smear over</i>, <i>besmear</i>,
				<i>anoint</i> with a thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">totum corpus bulbis contritis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 3, 19, 19</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To smear</i> or <i>spread</i> a thing
				<i>over</i> another: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">idque superillitum panniculo imponendum est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					6, 18, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">superinlito butyro ovillo cum melle,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					30, 12, 37, § 111</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sucus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Herb. 74</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
